  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Diasporas&#x2019; Operations and Coordination in Humanitarian Assistance for Increased Impact within a Framework for Diaspora Engagement in Humanitarian Assistance &#x2013; Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over the last few years, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) and other key humanitarian actors, such as the Danish Refugee Council through the Diaspora Emergency Action &amp; Coordination (DEMAC), have progressed significantly towards further strengthening diasporas&#x2019; engagement in humanitarian assistance as well as identifying and testing entry points and pathways to promote more effective communication, coordination, and cooperation between Diaspora Organizations (DOs) and other institutional humanitarian actors in real crisis settings, and in line with the guidance provided by IOM&#x2019;s Framework for Diaspora&#x2019;s Engagement in Humanitarian Assistance. 
 
This project sustains and is advancing this work by further exploring concrete examples and evidence of the impact of diasporas&#x2019; humanitarian interventions, especially as enhanced by internal and external coordination, and or while promoting additional applications of the framework and compatible coordination systems in current and emerging crises, including those affected by climate change. IOM and DEMAC continue to increase engagement and visibility for DOs in the humanitarian system through provision of learning, research, exchange, and accompaniment. Also, the scaling-up of diaspora engagement is being promoted through support and encouragement of emerging diaspora leaders in humanitarianism, more systematic initiatives of peer-to-peer support, continued capacity building, and interface with other institutional humanitarian actors.</narrative>
  </description>
